/*
*ANY new Layers get defined in here along with an assigned color. New formats are defined below, we no longer have to use the "standard" ZMK formatting, and can add to the code much easier using these new syntaxes and variables. I set up a "template" for your use in the appropriate areas, so you can better understand the layouts of this file.

Order of Operations:
    Just #define a layer
    then #define the color for the layer
    Build your macros, THEN build your hold-tap behavior if needed.
    Then you can use these new behaviors in ZMK Studio

New modular structuring-
 #define MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(node_name, node_label, layer, NEWCOLOR, DEFAULT_COLOR)
    This macro defines the "new" momentary layer's color 
       
 #define RGB_HOLD_TAP(node_name, node_label, macro_ref)
    This behavior defines the "new" momentary layer macro's function; used in conjunction with the above to get momentary LEDs

            Making a momentary layer: 
                    1. Define the layer
                    1a. Define the RGB color
                    2. Build the MACRO using 
                        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(node_name, "ZMK_Studio_Description", LAYER_, NEWCOLOR, DEFAULT_COLOR)
                    3. Build the BEHAVIOR using
                        RGB_HOLD_TAP(node_name, node_label, macro_ref)
                    4. Map the new BEHAVIOR node_name into your .keymap

                - Making a TOGGLED Layer uses a similar approach (not to be confused with a "ToggleLayer" which is the "menu" to access a TOGGLED LAYER. i.e TGLR1 & 2 CANNOT be activated until we are on the ToggleLayer) but instead we use:
                    TO_RGB_MACRO(node_name, "ZMK_Studio_Description", LAYER_, NEWCOLOR)
                    Then map the new macro node_name to our keymap, either in your files or ZMK.Studio

                - Making a ToggleLayer (GAMETGL & TGL)
                 Is used mostly exclusively for ToggleLayers since the RGB behaves differently on ToggleLayers when switching to a TOGGLED LAYER. 
                        TO_RGB_PRESS_MACRO(node_name, "ZMK_Studio_Description", LAYER_, NEWCOLOR)
                I personally use these on combos so that way we can have a "hidden" out of the way ToggleLayer activation, and it makes navigating between different Base Layers much more accessible. I was also having an isssue making the TOGGLED LAYERS rgbs work properly due to my naive/no understanding of programming so I just opted for the more direct approach.
                                    COMBO -> MENU -> SELECTED LAYER
                                    SAME COMBO -> BACK MENU OR PRESS AGAIN -> "BASE" LAYER (In the base layer there's a gameCombo, then in the game combo we can go back to the base layer, OR press the ToggleLayer Combo to access the GAMEToggleLayer, then from the GAMEToggleLayer we can press the gameCombo again to go back to the game layer and if the same combo is pressed again from the game it will bring us back to our BaseLayer. Showcasing same combos providing different functions depending on how we code the layer conditons for the combo; which is an important design for getting the RGBs to change fluidly and to not over convolute the keypresses. Path the combos to fit your layouts)


So now we can think about our layers in 3 ways: Is it a BaseLayer? (a layer that you want to "stay on")
                                                Is it a ToggleLayer? (a layer that's only function is exclusively used to "toggle" a different BaseLayer)
                                                Is it a MomentaryLayer? (a layer that acts only on a BaseLayer when a key press is held)
                                        This will help you understand which Macros, Behaviors, and Combos to utilize building your RGB Layers
*/



// 1. DEFINE LAYERS:
// Defined layers, this is done first; instead of numbers we can use a "layer name" variable to make the code easier to address. For any new layer(s) you just change the number(s), make sure the number matches with the corrosponding layer in the keymap, everything is in sequence starting from 0.
#define LAYER_ABC 0
#define LAYER_NMRW 1
#define LAYER_KPAD 2
#define LAYER_XTRA 3
#define LAYER_XTR2 4
#define LAYER_GAME 5
#define LAYER_GFUN 6
#define LAYER_GAMETGL 7 
#define LAYER_GAME2 8
#define LAYER_TGL 9
#define LAYER_TGLLR_1 10
#define LAYER_TGLLR_2 11
#define LAYER_TGLLR_2_SUBLLR_1 12

// 1a. DEFINE THE COLOR:
// Get color codes here https://colorizer.org/
// Dedicated Layer Colors, this defines a color using easaily identifiable variables instead of the code RGB_COLOR_HSB().
        // LAYOUT (COLOR, HUE, BRIGHTNESS)
// #define RGB_LAYERNAME RGB_COLOR_HSB(0,0,0)
// Personally I use a brighter setting for my momentary/toggle layers, and then use a dimmer one for the "BASE" layers depending on the color intensity.
#define RGB_ABC RGB_COLOR_HSB(19,100,17) // Dim Yellow BASELAYER COLOR
#define RGB_NMRW RGB_COLOR_HSB(183,45,18) // Teal
#define RGB_KPAD RGB_COLOR_HSB(230,87,26) // Pale Blue 
#define RGB_XTRA RGB_COLOR_HSB(273,67,23) // Light Purple
#define RGB_GAME RGB_COLOR_HSB(0,100,25) // Dim Red
#define RGB_GAMETGL RGB_COLOR_HSB(200,100,60) // Bright MC Diamonds
#define RGB_G2 RGB_COLOR_HSB(73,67,15) // Dim Emerald
#define RGB_GFUN RGB_COLOR_HSB(116,67,50) // Bright Yellow
#define RGB_XTRA2 RGB_COLOR_HSB(116,67,26) // Pale Green
#define RGB_TGL RGB_COLOR_HSB(251,67,50) // Bright Indigo
#define RGB_TGLLR_1 RGB_COLOR_HSB(40,100,12) // Dim Yellow TGLLR2 BASE COLOR
#define RGB_TGLLR_2 RGB_COLOR_HSB(85,100,15) // Dim  Lime TGLLR2 BASE COLOR
#define RGB_TGLLR_2_SUBLLR_1 RGB_COLOR_HSB(82,100,50) // Bright Lime  
//

//TEST
/* Blink with configurable colors */
#define BLINK_ON  RGB_COLOR_HSB(39,100,75)   /* activation color */
#define BLINK_OFF RGB_COLOR_HSB(273,67,23)   /* fallback color goes to xtra layer color but that doesnt seem to affect the RGBs if pressed quickly*/
#define BLINK_ON2 RGB_COLOR_HSB(0,0,0)  /* EXTRA activation color */
#define BLINK_OFF2 RGB_COLOR_HSB(0,0,0)      /* EXTRA fallback/default */

#define N_BLINK_ON RGB_COLOR_HSB(0,100,60)  /* activation color */
#define N_BLINK_OFF RGB_COLOR_HSB(19,100,17)    /* fallback/default */

#define C_BLINK_ON RGB_COLOR_HSB(200,100,60)
#define C_BLINK_OFF RGB_COLOR_HSB(19,100,17)  /* fallback/default */

#define BLINK_SEQ(ON, OFF, WAIT) \
        &macro_tap       &rgb_ug ON \
        &macro_wait_time WAIT       \
        &macro_tap       &rgb_ug RGB_TOG \
        &macro_wait_time WAIT       \
        &macro_tap       &rgb_ug RGB_TOG \
        &macro_wait_time WAIT       \
        &macro_tap       &rgb_ug OFF \

// NEW MACRO FORMAT:
// Restructured Macros, here we redefined the macros to a new 'layout', we can use the above definitons to create a macro below. This give more modularity since we only have to define our variables now for the layers. There is no need to build this code anymore since our variables are now handling it.
#define MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(node_name, node_label, layer, active_color, release_color) \
        ZMK_MACRO(node_name, \
            bindings = \
                <&macro_press>, \
                <&mo layer>, \
                <&macro_tap>, \
                <&rgb_ug active_color>, \
                <&macro_pause_for_release>, \
                <&macro_release>, \
                <&mo layer>, \
                <&macro_tap>, \
                <&rgb_ug release_color>; \
            label = node_label; \
        )

#define TO_RGB_MACRO(node_name, node_label, layer, color) \
        ZMK_MACRO(node_name, \
            bindings = \
                <&macro_tap>, \
                <&to layer>, \
                <&macro_tap>, \
                <&rgb_ug color>; \
            label = node_label; \
        )
#define TO_RGB_PRESS_MACRO(node_name, node_label, layer, color) \
        ZMK_MACRO(node_name, \
            bindings = \
                <&macro_tap>, \
                <&to layer>, \
                <&macro_press>, \
                <&rgb_ug color>; \
            label = node_label; \
        )   
        // New Behavior Structure
#define RGB_HOLD_TAP(node_name, node_label, macro_ref) \
        node_name: node_name { \
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap"; \
            label = node_label; \
            bindings = <&macro_ref>, <&kp>; \
            #binding-cells = <2>; \
            tapping-term-ms = <180>; \
            flavor = "tap-preferred"; \
        };
// #define BLINK_MACRO(node_name, node_label, KP, blink_color, back_color) \
//           ZMK_MACRO(node_name
//                bindings = \
//                <&macro_tap>, \
//                <&kp>, \
//                <&rgb_ug blink_color>, \
//                <&macro_pause_for_release>, \
//                <&rgb_ug back_color>; \
//              label = node_label;
//        )

/ {
    behaviors {
        hm: homerow_mods {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "HOMEROW_MODS";
            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <200>;
            quick_tap_ms = <0>;
            flavor = "tap-preferred";
            bindings = <&kp>, <&kp>;

            quick-tap-ms = <180>;
            global-quick-tap;
        };

        ltq: ltq {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-hold-tap";
            label = "LTQ";
            bindings = <&mo>, <&kp>;

            #binding-cells = <2>;
            tapping-term-ms = <600>;
            global-quick-tap;
            quick-tap-ms = <400>;
        };
// 2. BEHAVIORS:
// These create a behavior for the momentary LEDs, macros should be made FIRST; This is made AFTER making RGB behaviors, for any momentary layers!
    //      RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_layername, "ZMK_Studio_Description", macro_led)

        RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_nmrw, "HOLD_TAP_NMRW", nmrw_led)
        RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_xtra2, "HOLD_TAP_XTRA2", xtra2_led)
        RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_kpad, "HOLD_TAP_KPAD", kpad_led)
        RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_xtra, "HOLD_TAP_XTRA", xtra_led)
        RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_gfun, "HOLD_TAP_GFUN", gfun_led)
        RGB_HOLD_TAP(hold_tap_t2_s1, "HOLD_TAP_layer2_sublayer1", t2_s1_led)



        };
        td_numcaps: td_numcapsBLINK {
            compatible = "zmk,behavior-tap-dance";
            #binding-cells = <0>;
            tapping-term-ms = <300>;
            bindings = <&kp LSFT>,   
                       <&caps_blink>,
                       <&num_blink>; 
         };      

    combos {
        compatible = "zmk,combos";

        left_bkt {
            bindings = <&kp LEFT_BRACKET>;
            key-positions = <4 3>;
            timeout-ms = <50>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;

        };

        right_bkt {
            bindings = <&kp RBKT>;
            key-positions = <7 8>;
            timeout-ms = <50>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;

        };

        left_par {
            bindings = <&kp LEFT_PARENTHESIS>;
            key-positions = <15 16>;
            timeout-ms = <50>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;

        };

        right_par {
            bindings = <&kp RIGHT_PARENTHESIS>;
            key-positions = <19 20>;
            timeout-ms = <50>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;

        };

        left_brace {
            bindings = <&kp LEFT_BRACE>;
            key-positions = <27 28>;
            timeout-ms = <50>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;

        };

        right_brace {
            bindings = <&kp RIGHT_BRACE>;
            key-positions = <32 31>;
            timeout-ms = <50>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;
    
        };

        bac {
            bindings = <&kp BACKSLASH>;
            key-positions = <5 6>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;

        };

        pipe {
            bindings = <&kp PIPE>;
            key-positions = <17 18>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC>;
        };
// Combo Activates the GameLayer on Layer(s): Base ToggleLayer Game2 GameToggleLayer 
        gameLayer {
            bindings = <&game_led>;
            key-positions = <0 11>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC LAYER_TGL LAYER_GAME2>;
        };
// Combo Activates the BaseLayer on Layer(s): Game
        gameLayer_2_BaseLayer {
            bindings = <&default_led>;
            key-positions = <0 11>;
            layers = <LAYER_GAME>;
        };
// Combo Activates the ToggleLayer on Layer(s): Base ToggleLayer1 ToggleLayer2
        toggleLayer {
            bindings = <&toglayers_leds>;
            key-positions = <38 39>;
            layers = <LAYER_ABC LAYER_TGLLR_1 LAYER_TGLLR_2>;
        };
// Combo Activates the BaseLayer on Layer(s): ToggleLayer 
        toggleLayer_2_defaultLayer {
            bindings = <&default_led>;
            key-positions = <39 38>;
            layers = <LAYER_TGL>;
        };
// Combo Activates the GameToggleLayer on Layer(s): Game Game2 
        game_toggle {
            bindings = <&gtgl_led>;
            key-positions = <38 39>;
            layers = <LAYER_GAME LAYER_GAME2>;
        };
// Combo Activates the GameLayer on Layer(s): Game
        game_toggle_2_game {
            bindings = <&game_led>;
            key-positions = <38 39>;
            layers = <LAYER_GAMETGL>;
        };
    };
// 1. MACROS: 
// Here is where you actually build the LED function with our new definitions. 
// We have 2 new definitions. TO_RGB_MACRO and MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO, use accoring to your needs.
// If using momentary then you will likely also be building a hold-tap behavior AFTER this. The hold_tap node should then be mapped to a key 
        //  TO_RGB_MACRO(node_name, "ZMK_Studio_Description", LAYER_, NEWCOLOR)
        //  MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(node_name, "ZMK_Studio_Description", LAYER_, NEWCOLOR, DEFAULT_COLOR)
    macros {
        TO_RGB_MACRO(game_led, "GameLayer LED Macro", LAYER_GAME, RGB_GAME)

        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(xtra2_led, "xtra2Layer Momentary LED Macro", LAYER_XTR2, RGB_XTRA2, RGB_ABC)

        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(kpad_led, "KeyPadLayer Momentary LED Macro", LAYER_KPAD, RGB_KPAD, RGB_ABC)

        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(xtra_led, "ExtraLayer Momentary LED Macro", LAYER_XTRA, RGB_XTRA, RGB_ABC)

        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(nmrw_led, "NumberRowLayer Momentary LED Macro", LAYER_NMRW, RGB_NMRW, RGB_ABC)

        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(gfun_led, "GameLayer Sublayer Momentary LED Macro", LAYER_GFUN, RGB_GFUN, RGB_GAME)

        TO_RGB_MACRO(default_led, "Base Layer LED", LAYER_ABC, RGB_ABC)

        TO_RGB_MACRO(t1_led, "ToggleLayer1 LED", LAYER_TGLLR_1, RGB_TGLLR_1)

        TO_RGB_MACRO(to_t2_led, "ToggleLayer2 LED", LAYER_TGLLR_2, RGB_TGLLR_2)

        MOMENTARY_RGB_MACRO(t2_s1_led, "ToggleLayer2 SubLayer1 Momentary LED Macro", LAYER_TGLLR_2_SUBLLR_1, RGB_TGLLR_2_SUBLLR_1, RGB_TGLLR_2)

        TO_RGB_MACRO(g2_led, "Game2 LED Macro", LAYER_GAME2, RGB_G2)

        //Toggle Layers
        TO_RGB_PRESS_MACRO(toglayers_leds, "ToggleLayer LED", LAYER_TGL, RGB_TGL)

        TO_RGB_PRESS_MACRO(gtgl_led, "gametoggle LED Macro", LAYER_GAMETGL, RGB_GAMETGL)

        // TEST
    };
    // ZMK Bindable
        blnk: blnk {
        compatible = "zmk,behavior-macro-one-param";
        label = "BLINK (key param)";
        #binding-cells = <1>;
        wait-ms = <0>;
        tap-ms  = <0>;

        bindings = <
            &macro_param_1to1
            &macro_tap &kp MACRO_PLACEHOLDER
            BLINK_SEQ(BLINK_ON, BLINK_OFF, 100)
    >;

    };
    caps_blink: caps_blink {
        compatible = "zmk,behavior-macro";
        label = "CAPS TOGGLE + BLINK";
        #binding-cells = <0>;
        bindings = <
            &macro_tap &kp CAPS
            BLINK_SEQ(C_BLINK_ON, C_BLINK_OFF, 80)
    >;
    };
    num_blink: num_blink {
        compatible = "zmk,behavior-macro";
        label = "NUM TOGGLE + BLINK";
        #binding-cells = <0>;
        bindings = <
            &macro_tap &kp KP_NUMLOCK
            BLINK_SEQ(N_BLINK_ON, N_BLINK_OFF, 80)
    >;

    };
};
